      "message": "IIUC this will make the stopTethering call synchronous across the board, so that it will take considerably longer than it used to. This includes ConnectivityManager#stopTethering.\n\nThis means all callers of this API are suddenly subject to a blocking call. Though this lives on the client side it can certainly ANR apps (e.g. Settings and QS in SystemUI are calling ConnectivityManager#stopTether on their main thread), and if there are any calls to this from the system server it can be really dangerous.",
